# In-file variables: '@name = value' lines apply to every request in the file
# and win over environment values with the same name.
@resource = anything
@sampleId = 1234

### Environment variable in the URL ({{baseUrl}} comes from http-client.env.json)
GET {{baseUrl}}/get?source=env-variables
Accept: application/json

### In-file @variables combined with env variables
POST {{baseUrl}}/{{resource}}/{{sampleId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "resourceUsed": "{{resource}}",
  "id": "{{sampleId}}"
}

### Built-in dynamic variables (new value on every run)
POST {{baseUrl}}/anything
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requestId": "{{$uuid}}",
  "unixSeconds": "{{$timestamp}}",
  "isoTime": "{{$isoTimestamp}}",
  "randomInt": "{{$randomInt}}"
}

### Multi-line URL — indented ?/& lines continue the request line
GET {{baseUrl}}/get
    ?page=2
    &pageSize=25
    &sort=name
Accept: application/json

### Unresolved variable — run WITHOUT an environment to see the warning banner
GET {{baseUrl}}/headers
X-Api-Key: {{iDoNotExistAnywhere}}
